  "summary_en": "Malaysian CAAM directive (Issue 01/Rev 01, Nov 2022) setting binding requirements and a five-phase approval process for Special UAS Project operations (BVLOS, carriage of dangerous goods, R&D). It adopts the JARUS SORA risk methodology, operator management and safety systems, UTM services, insurance, and occurrence reporting, and prohibits autonomous operations.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No person may conduct Special UAS Project operations without a valid CAAM SUP Approval, valid up to one year.",
   "Operational risk assessment via JARUS SORA determines SAIL and operational safety objectives; SAIL III and above need the full five-phase process.",
   "Autonomous operations (no remote pilot ability to intervene) are not allowed.",
   "Operators must hold third-party liability insurance, a UTM service, an accountable manager and a safety management system.",
   "Dangerous goods carriage needs a separate CAAM application, extra risk assessment and a DG SOP; contraventions are offences under the Civil Aviation Act 1969."
  ],
